# OpenHR data.
#
# data/openhr.db IS tracked: it ships the seeded demo company so the repo is
# runnable the moment it is cloned, without a seed step. It contains only the
# fictional dataset from scripts/seed.py — never point OPENHR_DB at a tracked
# file when working with real employee records.
#
# Regenerate it with `python scripts/seed.py`. Because it is a tracked binary,
# any local run that writes to it (the smoke test does) will show up as a
# modified file; re-seed before committing, or `git checkout -- data/openhr.db`
# to discard the churn.
data/*.db
!data/openhr.db

# SQLite sidecar files are always local — never commit these.
data/*.db-journal
data/*.db-wal
data/*.db-shm

